rear-tail lift/dip, not a horizontal wag or body action. The unchanged Tail bone runs from normalized[.40,.83,.22] to[.19,.94,.22], parent Pelvis, with the existing feathered Tail/Pelvis layer. Native v2 reported1685 original vertices with Tail weight; its exported body includes1767 weighted vertices after attribute splits,1667 over half Tail weight. The rear corrected stalk remains Tail/Pelvis owned and never becomes a shoulder-companion attachment.\nAmplitude selection used bounded pure rest-space estimates from the ACTUAL exported v2 body positions, triangle edges and skin weights: Head-Y±3.5degrees gives~33mm maximum vertex movement and6.5–8.5mm thresholded worst edge excess; Tail-Y±4degrees gives~22mm tip movement, with no thresholded row in one direction and~8.4mm worst edge excess in the other. Larger Tail-Z±10degree trials were not authored because estimated seam excess reached21–27mm. These are numerical screening estimates, not native rendering, self-intersection checks or semantic acceptance.\nNo explicit arm, pelvis, root or foot animation channels are added; the preserved idle includes only its existing tiny torso/head settling. New actions move only Head or Tail, with no props, fingers, locomotion, rewards, physics or hair dynamics. Endpoints return to rest but loop certification remains false. Render and independently inspect each new motion before claiming it works visually; no human approval, original Muse reconstruction, Muse-quality parity or frozen-profile Weft compatibility is claimed.",
